{"key":"enterprise/T1197","id":"T1197","name":"BITS Jobs","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["execution","persistence","stealth"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse BITS jobs to persistently execute code and perform various background tasks. Windows Background Intelligent Transfer Service (BITS) is a low-bandwidth, asynchronous file transfer mechanism exposed through Component Object Model (COM). BITS is commonly used by updaters, messengers, and other applications preferred to operate in the background (using available idle bandwidth) without interrupting other networked applications.…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1197","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--c8e87b83-edbb-48d4-9295-4974897525b7","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.716Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0060","name":"Service Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0060","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5297a638-1382-4f0c-8472-0d21830bf705","page":"telemetry/DC0060/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0098","name":"Detect abuse of Windows BITS Jobs for download, execution and persistence","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0098","stix_id":"